  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a *positive* number `n`.\n\nOutput the **smallest** number `x` **greater than** or **equal to** `n`, such that the binary representation of `x` includes only set bits\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** n = 5\n\n**Output:** 7\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe binary representation of 7 is `\"111\"`.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** n = 10\n\n**Output:** 15\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe binary representation of 15 is `\"1111\"`.\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n**Input:** n = 3\n\n**Output:** 3\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe binary representation of 3 is `\"11\"`.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= n <= 1000`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
